---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Motif Movement">
  <section class="pt-10 sm:pt-14">
    <h2 class="font-[Space_Grotesk,system-ui,sans-serif] text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">About</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg">
      <p>
        The Motif Movement is a bass collective by the people, of the people, for the people. We formed to
        create a safe, high quality, and immersive space for all walks of life to listen to the bone shaking
        music that brought us all together. We take pride in our high fidelity Paraflex system, one of the
        best sounding rigs in West Texas. Regardless of if it's a warehouse show, a full venue, or a
        soundcamp at a festival we aim to provide a top level experience that is guaranteed to have you shake
        a tail feather.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our roster is comprised of some of the best artists in the 806, and we are excited for the
        opportunity to share that art with all of you!
      </p>
      <p>
        Producer/DJs such as <strong class="text-neutral-100">Big-A</strong>,{" "}
        <strong class="text-neutral-100">Bass Slave</strong>, and{" "}
        <strong class="text-neutral-100">Mask</strong> help push our scene forward with their original music,
        uniquely crafted sets, and thoughtful sonic innovations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Visual artists such as <strong class="text-neutral-100">Lucid_Vision</strong> and{" "}
        <strong class="text-neutral-100">Ne0n Croissant</strong> help bring the show to life with immersive
        and interactive visuals, stage design, lights, lasers...and a fair amount of pixie dust.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="font-[Space_Grotesk,system-ui,sans-serif] text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold pt-12 mt-4">
      The Paraflex System
    </h3>

    <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="aspect-[4/3] bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <img
          src="/customer-assets/Paraflex%20system%20pics/1000020264.jpg"
          alt="Motif Paraflex rig"
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="aspect-[4/3] bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <img
          src="/customer-assets/Paraflex%20system%20pics/L%20stack.jpg"
          alt="L-stack configuration"
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="aspect-[4/3] bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <img
          src="/customer-assets/Paraflex%20system%20pics/Single%20stack%20flex.jpg"
          alt="Single stack flex"
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg">
      <p>
        High quality sound is always our number one priority and comes before anything else that we do. We
        knew we wanted something unique and powerful, but also portable enough to be able to share our sound
        with surrounding areas as we continue to grow. For our system owners (Caleb, Carson, and Jesse),
        bone-shaking bass is a non-negotiable requirement — but not at the expense of surgical imaging and
        technical accuracy in the high end.
      </p>
      <p>
        To ensure we retained maximum bass without sacrificing high end fidelity, we turned to{" "}
        <strong class="text-neutral-100">WAAT Audio</strong>, a leader in the paraflex construction and
        distribution space. We then expanded on our initial investment and eventually pieced together a
        powerhouse of a rig that was built, tested, and tuned by the professionals at WAAT. For every new
        deployment our sound engineers tune and dial in the rig so that we provide sound that can be felt
        deep in your chest WITHOUT blowing out your eardrums.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h4 class="font-[Space_Grotesk,system-ui,sans-serif] text-lg font-bold text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Subwoofers
        </h4>
        <ul class="text-sm text-neutral-400 space-y-1.5">
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">(4)</span> Paraflex 21 ELF Subwoofers</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Driver:</span> B&C 21SW152-4 (4-ohm)</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Power:</span> 2000W AES</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Voice coil:</span> 4.5", neodymium motor</li>
          <li class="text-neutral-500 text-xs pt-1">Extended Low Frequency 6th-order bandpass</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h4 class="font-[Space_Grotesk,system-ui,sans-serif] text-lg font-bold text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Mid-Bass / Kick
        </h4>
        <ul class="text-sm text-neutral-400 space-y-1.5">
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">(2)</span> Paraflex C2D "Kicktops" (C3D112)</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Driver:</span> HOQS N123 Neo 12"</li>
          <li class="text-neutral-500 text-xs pt-1">High-sensitivity neodymium, horn-loaded</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-neutral-900 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h4 class="font-[Space_Grotesk,system-ui,sans-serif] text-lg font-bold text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          High Frequency
        </h4>
        <ul class="text-sm text-neutral-400 space-y-1.5">
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">(2)</span> BH1 60° × 40° CD horns</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Driver:</span> HF143N 1.4" exit</li>
          <li><span class="text-neutral-200">Magnet:</span> Neodymium, 3" voice coil</li>
          <li class="text-neutral-500 text-xs pt-1">Clean output above crossover</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
